  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340660",
      "title": "Handling Errors With Error Pages",
      "lectureOrder": 145,
      "videoOrder": 135,
      "sourceHash": "5208f4b39a6a82bcc716db1f06c9c6465caa812fd628eec28f7c127c0a0d352a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 1.65,
          "en": "Let's now make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.65,
          "end": 3.99,
          "en": "that we handle this error on our own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 3.99,
          "end": 7.98,
          "en": "with our own error fallback content instead of using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.98,
          "end": 11.58,
          "en": "that default development mode overlay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.58,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "And we can handle errors in NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 19.05,
          "en": "by adding a special file named error.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.05,
          "end": 22.65,
          "en": "and it works just like the not-found.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.65,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "We can add it anywhere and it will then render its component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 29.19,
          "en": "whenever an error occurs on the same level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.19,
          "end": 31.143,
          "en": "or in some nested page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.19,
          "end": 35.61,
          "en": "So here to handle errors for this page.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.61,
          "end": 38.943,
          "en": "we could add an error.js file right next to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.84,
          "end": 43.65,
          "en": "And then here I'll have my default function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.65,
          "end": 48.12,
          "en": "FilterError could be the component function name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.12,
          "end": 51.72,
          "en": "And then there I'll return a div with an id of error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.72,
          "end": 56.28,
          "en": "with an h2 element of an error occurred",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.28,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 62.55,
          "en": "And then I'll have a text here where I say invalid path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.55,
          "end": 64.56,
          "en": "And of course, it's totally up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.56,
          "end": 66.333,
          "en": "how you wanna configure this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.59,
          "end": 69.57,
          "en": "What's important though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.57,
          "end": 73.35,
          "en": "is that this now must be a client component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.35,
          "end": 77.94,
          "en": "which you do ensure by adding use client at the top here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.94,
          "end": 80.85,
          "en": "Now, this error.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.85,
          "end": 83.31,
          "en": "or the component you return in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.31,
          "end": 85.26,
          "en": "must be a client component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.26,
          "end": 89.46000000000001,
          "en": "and hence you must add use client to the top of this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.46000000000001,
          "end": 92.61,
          "en": "because errors can, of course, not just occur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.61,
          "end": 95.67,
          "en": "whilst something's happening on this server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.67,
          "end": 98.55,
          "en": "but they may also occur from the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.55,
          "end": 102.42,
          "en": "because something goes wrong after the page was loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.42,
          "end": 105.53999999999999,
          "en": "and after the user is using the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.53999999999999,
          "end": 109.62,
          "en": "And therefore, the error fallback needs to work on both ends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.62,
          "end": 113.49000000000001,
          "en": "and client components do work on both ends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.49000000000001,
          "end": 116.00999999999999,
          "en": "on the Server, but also on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.00999999999999,
          "end": 119.95,
          "en": "Whereas server components without use client at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.053,
          "end": 122.82,
          "en": "of the file would only work on the server side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.82,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "That's why this error fallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 129.81,
          "en": "must be a client component and hence you must add use client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.81,
          "end": 131.223,
          "en": "at the top of the file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.15,
          "end": 134.64,
          "en": "And I'll get back to client components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.64,
          "end": 138.18,
          "en": "and server components a little bit later again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.18,
          "end": 140.7,
          "en": "I did also cover this important topic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.7,
          "end": 143.073,
          "en": "in the essentials section already though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.09,
          "end": 147.69,
          "en": "So with that we have this FilterError function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.69,
          "end": 150.57,
          "en": "and this now actually also receives some props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.57,
          "end": 153.483,
          "en": "which are passed in by NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.32,
          "end": 157.3,
          "en": "For example, the error object that was thrown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.16,
          "end": 162,
          "en": "so that we could also output the actual error.message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162,
          "end": 165.273,
          "en": "instead of invalid path if we wanted to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.41,
          "end": 167.94,
          "en": "With that, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.94,
          "end": 172.94,
          "en": "you see that now I get my own error fallback here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.28,
          "end": 176.13,
          "en": "and I can continue using the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.13,
          "end": 180.183,
          "en": "and basically leave that error state.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
